{
  "project_name": "codemonkey",
  "programming_languages": [
    "Python"
  ],
  "summary": "CodeMonkey is a scriptable coding-agent CLI (Python 3.11, built with uv, Typer, Rich, and httpx) that runs against OpenAI-style (/v1/chat/completions) and Anthropic-style (/v1/messages) LLM endpoints, including local llama.cpp servers. It offers an interactive REPL when run bare and a non-interactive `codemonkey exec` mode with machine-readable JSONL event streams, structured output via JSON schema, session resume, stdin piping, sandbox/approval semantics modeled on `codex exec`, YAML/.env-based multi-provider configuration, a typical coding-agent tool set (shell, file read/write/edit, search, glob, plan updates, web fetch), and a pluggable strategy architecture for compaction, memory, and session state."
}
